# Example environment variables.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (repo root) and fill in real values:  cp .env.example .env
# `.env` is gitignored and must NEVER be committed. Only this example file,
# with placeholder values, belongs in version control. See workflow/principles.md.
#
# The backend loads it with Node's --env-file-if-exists, so `.env` is optional.
# The current scaffold needs no variables. Each feature adds the ones it uses here,
# with a placeholder value (planned: see "Configuration" in docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).
